# =============================================================================
# FSEXIT SUITE (2026-10-01) - a mouse way out of a dashboard chart tile's fullscreen
#
# A dashboard chart tile is the report's chart carousel in a same-origin frame
# (index.php?embed=1&fullscreen=true&fspages=N), opened PERSISTENT: the overlay
# IS the tile, so every close path no-ops and main.css hides the x. The tile's
# fullscreen button (U+26F6, shown on hover) puts it in native fullscreen, and
# until 2026-10-01 the only way back was the keyboard (Esc). Now, in native
# fullscreen, the x shows in its usual corner (main.css:
# #chartCarouselOverlay.cc-persistent:fullscreen .cc-close) named "Exit
# fullscreen (Esc)", and close() LEAVES fullscreen for a persistent overlay:
# the tile stays and the fullscreen button is offered again. A report's own
# fullscreen x still closes the carousel.
#
# FSFIT (2026-10-01, same day): report charts RE-FIT. Both carousel mounts size
# the page from the viewport at that moment, and only tiles (persistent) and
# slides followed later changes - so a click-launched carousel, mounted before
# the browser granted fullscreen, kept the WINDOW's size: empty bands above and
# below in the fullscreen stage. Now the first mount of a click-launched
# carousel waits for the fullscreen request to settle (granted or refused, 1 s
# at most) and mounts ONCE at the final size, and every overlay re-mounts its
# chart page when the viewport settles at a new size (resize.ccFit, 200 ms; a
# report's slides keep their own re-scale), without restarting the countdown.
#
# Real fullscreen needs a user gesture, so this drives headless Edge over CDP
# with TRUSTED mouse/key events (Input.dispatch*), the REAL main.js + main.css,
# and a dashboard stand-in (host.html) framing the report page (tile.html).
# Scenarios (each a fresh tab):
#   tile    the fullscreen button, then the x, back to the tile - twice
#   kiosk   host.html fullscreen first (the dashboard's kiosk view): the tile's
#           x unwinds ONLY the tile; the kiosk stays fullscreen
#   esc     the tile fullscreen, then Escape (the keyboard way, unchanged)
#   report  report.html, not an embed: a click-launched carousel in true
#           fullscreen; its x closes the carousel (unchanged) and unbinds
#   fit     report.html: a click-launched carousel lands in fullscreen at the
#           fullscreen size, mounted once
#   win     report.html?charts=2: a carousel opened with NO gesture (refused,
#           windowed - the autoload path) re-fits when the viewport shrinks and
#           grows back (CDP device-metrics override) and after its fullscreen
#           button; the 4 s slideshow keeps its schedule through a re-fit
# Asserts:
#   T-mount  the tile's overlay is up, persistent, its chart drawn
#   T-nox    no x in the tile (nothing to close to)
#   T-offer  the fullscreen button is offered (cc-fs-denied) and shows on hover
#   T-fs     a click on it: the tile's overlay is the fullscreen element
#   T-x      in fullscreen the x is displayed, opaque, on screen, on top
#   T-name   ...and named "Exit fullscreen" / "Exit fullscreen (Esc)"
#   T-exit   a click on the x leaves fullscreen (tile AND host)
#   T-stay   ...and the tile stays: overlay + chart up, the button re-offered, the x hidden
#   T-again  a second round behaves the same
#   K-kiosk  the host's own fullscreen is granted (kiosk stand-in)
#   K-fs     the tile goes fullscreen inside it
#   K-x      the x is displayed there too
#   K-exit   a click on it leaves the TILE's fullscreen only: the host stays fullscreen, the tile stays
#   E-win    a windowed Escape that reaches the tile (the frame has focus) leaves the overlay up
#   E-fs     (precondition) the tile is fullscreen
#   E-exit   Escape leaves fullscreen and the tile stays (the browser keeps that Esc from the page)
#   R-fs     report page: a click-launched carousel (not persistent) is in true fullscreen
#   R-x      its x is displayed and named "Close" / "Close (Esc)"
#   R-close  a click on it closes the carousel and leaves fullscreen
#   R-unbind ...and no carousel resize handler is left on the window
#   T-fit    the tile's chart fills its stage in fullscreen and again back in the tile
#   F-fs     fit: the click-launched carousel is in true fullscreen
#   F-size   its chart fills the FULLSCREEN stage (chart vs the stage's content box)
#   F-once   ...mounted once (one entry animation, no re-mount after the resize)
#   W-open   win: refused + windowed, the chart fills the stage, one mount
#   W-shrink the viewport shrinks: the chart re-fits the smaller stage
#   C-keep   the re-fit did not restart the countdown: page 2 at ~4 s after the open
#   W-grow   the viewport grows back: the chart re-fits again
#   W-fs     its fullscreen button: the chart re-fits the fullscreen stage
#   *-err    no page errors (tile + host / report)
#
#   py -3 run.py                    candidate = the LIVE js\main.js + css\main.css
#   py -3 run.py --app <dir>        candidate = <dir>\js\main.js + <dir>\css\main.css (a stage)
#   py -3 run.py --control          the build before FSFIT (live main.js while it lacks the fix, else the
#                                   newest js\main.js.bak-*-fsfit; live main.css): RED on exactly CONTROL_RED
#   py -3 run.py --control-fsexit   the build before FSEXIT (js\main.js.bak-*-fsexit + css\main.css.bak-*-fsexit):
#                                   RED on exactly CONTROL_RED_FSEXIT
#   py -3 run.py --mutants          every mutant of the candidate against the asserts it must turn red
#   py -3 run.py --mutant NAME      one of them;  --explore prints the raw observations
# Headless Edge over CDP; stages into %TEMP%; writes nothing to the webroot.
# cd into this folder first (Git Bash mangles a \\server\d$ argument to py -3).
# =============================================================================
